# Datasets — directory-level, belt-and-braces (added 2026-08-07).
# The suffix rules above only catch KNOWN extensions; a dataset arriving with any
# other suffix (.zip, .tar.gz, .arrow, .bam, .fcs, …) would still be swept up by
# `git add -A`. That is how ~100 GB of h5ad-sized blobs once ended up loose in
# .git. So: ignore everything under data/ by default, then re-include only the
# small reference tables this repo genuinely tracks.
#   `data/*` (not `data/`) is required — git will not descend into an excluded
#   directory, so a bare `data/` would make the `!` lines below unreachable.
data/*
!data/*.csv
!data/LRdatabase/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
